	// The traits settlers are born with, Project Zomboid style. Every settler has at least one good trait
	// (points above 0) and one bad one (points below 0); quirks have 0 points. Each trait has a level
	// from 0 to 20 (config TraitLevelMax): a good trait's effect grows 5% a level, a bad trait's
	// penalty shrinks 4% a level, so a higher level is always better for the settler.
	//
	// Effects: a value like 1.15 on a "speed" key is a multiplier (15% faster), one like 0.8 is 20% slower.
	// Other keys add to the game's number: maxHealth 6 is six more health, sleepEnd 2 wakes two hours later.
	// Multiplier keys: workSpeed, walkSpeed, hunger, downedDays, regen, toolWear, variety, willpowerWait,
	// swingSpeed, nightSwing, pairAfter, packSlots, learning (all skill XP), decay (skill decay). Adding keys:
	// maxHealth, reckless, guardRange, retreatHealth, damageAdd, sleepStart, sleepEnd, childChance, freeBlock,
	// cookLevel, mood (happiness points). Flags (1 = on): noPair, pairFirst, flees, incapable-<skill> (can
	// never learn that skill or take its jobs).
	// "job": the trait only works while the settler has that job; a settler has at most one job trait.
	// "weight": how often it rolls. "inherited": children can get it from a parent. "earned": never rolled,
	// only given by the game (Veteran after kills, Shaken after knock-outs). "conflicts": never together.
